# Auth

Canonical: `docs/auth.md`. Cookies `dw_*` (renamed from ChainWise `cw_*`). `get_current_user` / `require_admin` stay; roles become `admin | manager | employee` plus `departments[]`.

```python
# ❌ BAD — client chooses visibility
def search(body: Query):
    roles = body.access_roles

# ✅ GOOD — server-side allowed_roles
def allowed_roles(user) -> list[str]:
    return list({user.role, *user.departments, "all"})
```

- Do not put `role` / `departments` in the request body as authorization input.
- KB write (upload/delete): `require_admin` only (manager cannot). Retrieval still uses document ACL; no admin override.
- Raw PDF bytes only after the same intersection check as `GET /documents`. Prefer `404` over confirming a hidden title.
- LLM Redis cache key must include the caller's `allowed_roles`.
